---
/**
 * HeroArtwork — «نشانه‌های پراکنده → سامانهٔ منظم» (Scattered Signal →
 * Structured System). The homepage's brand artwork (docs/DESIGN.md §3.6).
 *
 * Ninth review (2026-10): recomposed as the hero's full visual field
 * instead of a small square floating in the left column. The plate is
 * larger (432 of 640 units, two thirds of the frame), the ambient 80px
 * field grid now lives on the hero section itself so the artwork and the
 * copy share one continuous surface, and the surrounding scatter field is
 * denser and directional: attention arrives from the right/top-right and
 * registers, left and bottom-left.
 *
 * Concept: incoming attention (rotated fragments, ticks, dots) settles
 * into an ordered field — a hairline "system plate" of registered squares
 * whose pattern converges on the Noveno mark drawn as a quiet attractor.
 * The transition is perceived through alignment, spacing and orientation —
 * never drawn as arrows, connectors, or labels.
 *
 * Uniquely Noveno:
 *  - the brand mark appears as a hairline structural motif inside the
 *    plate, with small green squares locked onto its key vertices;
 *  - the plate carries registration ticks at its corners (the site's own
 *    hairline / square grammar), not a decorative frame;
 *  - colors are pure semantic tokens (text/line/line-strong/primary), so
 *    the artwork re-themes itself with Light/Dark.
 *
 * Motion (docs/DESIGN.md §12 family — transform/opacity only):
 *  - a handful of transition marks quietly settle into alignment;
 *  - the plate surface materializes once, and one registered square
 *    blinks an acknowledgment after load;
 *  - the registration sweep: after the settle, one hairline scan with a
 *    small `primary` lead square crosses the plate once (right → left,
 *    900ms, 1150ms) and the acknowledgment follows it;
 *  - tiny pointer parallax (two layers, ≤6px) on fine-pointer desktop
 *    only; prefers-reduced-motion renders the fully settled frame.
 *
 * The static first frame is the settled composition: nothing about the
 * artwork's quality depends on animation. No raster, no remote asset, no
 * library — the whole piece is one inline SVG per variant.
 *
 * Two variants: the square desktop field and a recomposed wide strip for
 * mobile (fewer, larger marks — never a shrunk desktop SVG).
 */

const MOTIF_PATH =
  "M266.458,392.827L124.074,174.407L63.904,318.218L0.5,317.995L114.581,51.524" +
  "L265.649,288.586C265.649,288.586 347.798,174.154 371.997,84.837L317.715,62.386" +
  "L263.782,84.45C263.782,84.45 269.742,147.856 313.528,163.292L284.862,214.638" +
  "C284.862,214.638 208.851,188.767 199.035,49.522L317.889,0.5L436.986,49.522" +
  "C436.986,49.522 436.866,152.092 266.458,392.827Z";
---

